# libcanberra -- plays desktop event sounds, and is what mutter's
# -Dsound_player=true resolves.
#
# mutter meson.build:190-193 gates it on have_sound_player, which defaults true,
# and then takes dependency('libcanberra', version: '>= 0.26'). This package is
# the player; the SOUNDS come from sound-theme-freedesktop, packaged alongside,
# and neither is any use without the other -- see the note there.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://0pointer.de/lennart/projects/libcanberra/libcanberra-0.30.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=c2b671e67e0c288a69fc33dc1b6f1b534d07882c2aceed37004bf48c601afa72
SRC_DIR=libcanberra-0.30

# NO PATCH, AND THAT IS A CORRECTION. This recipe first carried BLFS 12.4's
# libcanberra-0.30-wayland-1.patch, on the reasoning that a patch whose header
# says "fix a bug crashing some applications in Wayland desktops" is not
# optional in a Wayland-first tree. That reasoning was right about the patch and
# wrong about this build: the patch touches src/canberra-gtk-module.c and
# src/canberra-gtk.c and NOTHING ELSE, and those two files are compiled only
# when the GTK helper is enabled -- which this recipe now disables, for the
# reason directly below. With --disable-gtk3 the patch is inert, so carrying it
# would leave a confident comment attached to a file that does nothing.
#
# IF THE GTK HELPER IS EVER ENABLED HERE, THAT PATCH MUST COME BACK.

# --disable-oss: OSS has not been the Linux audio interface for twenty years and
# BLFS disables it too.
#
# --disable-gstreamer and --disable-pulse. BOTH DEFAULT TO **auto** in
# configure.ac (the gstreamer block at 375, pulse at 301), and neither is
# packaged here, so both would silently resolve to "off" on their own. Pinned
# because a soft-skip that happens to do what is wanted is not a decision --
# and because if a gstreamer stack is ever packaged for something else, this
# would quietly grow a dependency on it without anyone choosing that.
#
# alsa is left ENABLED, its default, and is the backend that actually plays
# sound here: alsa-lib is packaged.
#
# --disable-gtk3 AND --disable-gtk, AND THIS IS THE CORRECTION THAT MATTERS.
#
# An earlier version of this recipe left --enable-gtk3 at its `auto` default and
# recorded the decision as examined: gtk3 IS packaged, the helper "costs one
# small library", and turning it off looked like a divergence from BLFS for no
# gain. CI disagreed on BOTH architectures:
#
#     src/canberra-gtk-module.c:28:10: fatal error: gdk/gdkx.h: No such file or directory
#
# gdk/gdkx.h is GTK 3's X11 BACKEND header, and this tree builds gtk3
# WAYLAND-ONLY (-Dx11_backend=false, packaged for libnma alone). So the helper
# is not merely unnecessary here, it is UNBUILDABLE here -- and only
# src/canberra-gtk-module.c and src/canberra-gtk.c include that header, which is
# why nothing else in the package noticed.
#
# The flaw in the original reasoning is worth keeping: it weighed the helper's
# PAYLOAD -- one small library, cheap either way -- and never asked what the
# helper LINKS AGAINST. An `auto` feature was examined for cost and not for
# compatibility, which is the same mistake as reading an option's existence
# instead of its default, one level along.
#
# Nothing in this tree uses ca_gtk_* in any case: mutter links plain
# libcanberra. --disable-gtk turns off the GTK 2 helper for the same reason,
# GTK 2 not being packaged at all.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-oss --disable-gstreamer --disable-pulse \
--disable-gtk3 --disable-gtk"
